<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-ciona-intestinalis-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Ciona intestinalis Turing wavelength at 51 µm (5.056e-05 m), Holocene 0 Ma (Ciona intestinalis)",
        "Ciona intestinalis Turing wavelength at 51 µm (5.056e-05 m), Holocene 0 Ma faithfully reproduces Ciona intestinalis morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-ciona-intestinalis-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-ciona-intestinalis-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-ciona-intestinalis-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-ciona-intestinalis-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-ciona-intestinalis-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Ciona intestinalis specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-ciona-intestinalis-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Ciona intestinalis" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a signed nanopublication. The profile file is absent, so trusty URIs were not minted.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the activator and inhibitor are identified Ciona molecules.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the adult tunic pattern is a 51 µm Turing field.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The GIF blend alpha is 0.50, the strongest weight that still ties the CV cap. The dispersion panel is limited to sigma in [-2, 1.2] so the unstable band is visible.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: gamma is solved so lambda_c = 5.056e-05 m at Dv/Du = 10. The ratio sweep moves analytical lambda from 57.0 µm to 48.6 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: Ciona pigment cells are a neural-crest-like lineage (Abitua et al. 2012). The larval ocellus and otolith sit in the sensory vesicle (Hudson 2016; Kourakis et al. 2021; Hotta et al. 2007).",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) derived the diffusion-driven instability and the critical wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) gave the two-species kinetic scheme used here.",
        "transfer_boundary: Adult pigment spacing 873 µm is not a measurement of the 51 µm law.",
        "transfer_boundary: Holocene chronoseries 1/1 has no temporal predecessor. Scale neighbours are a 1 µm melanosome and the adult body (measured length 34.0 mm)." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Ciona intestinalis" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Zoophyta & Vermes (Cnidaria/Platyhelminthes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Ciona" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-ciona-intestinalis-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/ciona_intestinalis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Ciona intestinalis; environment: python 3.12.3, note numpy, scipy, pillow, matplotlib. Signing skipped: ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent.; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) derived the diffusion-driven instability and the critical wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) gave the two-species kinetic scheme used here. | Ciona pigment cells are a neural-crest-like lineage (Abitua et al. 2012). The larval ocellus and otolith sit in the sensory vesicle (Hudson 2016; Kourakis et al. 2021; Hotta et al. 2007).; reconstructed_in_script: gamma is solved so lambda_c = 5.056e-05 m at Dv/Du = 10. The ratio sweep moves analytical lambda from 57.0 µm to 48.6 µm. | The GIF blend alpha is 0.50, the strongest weight that still ties the CV cap. The dispersion panel is limited to sigma in [-2, 1.2] so the unstable band is visible.; transfer_boundary: Holocene chronoseries 1/1 has no temporal predecessor. Scale neighbours are a 1 µm melanosome and the adult body (measured length 34.0 mm). | Adult pigment spacing 873 µm is not a measurement of the 51 µm law.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the activator and inhibitor are identified Ciona molecules. | Does not claim the adult tunic pattern is a 51 µm Turing field. | Does not claim a signed nanopublication. The profile file is absent, so trusty URIs were not minted.]; phenomenon_size: 46 µm (4.608e-05 m, log10=-4.336 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 46 µm to 14.4 cm): 46 µm:ciona-intestinalis-bioelectric-polarity, 172 µm:ciona-intestinalis-vertex-packing, 3.2 mm:ciona-intestinalis-turing-wavelength, 6.0 mm:ciona-intestinalis-clock-wavefront, 1.4 cm:ciona-intestinalis-elastic-buckling, 1.8 cm:ciona-intestinalis-morphogen-condensation, 2.4 cm:ciona-intestinalis-flux-canalization, 3.2 cm:ciona-intestinalis-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.21188>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1002/wdev.239>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
